---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const canonical = new URL(withBase('/work/yhct'), Astro.site).href;
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@type': 'Article',
    '@id': `${canonical}#case-study`,
    headline: 'YHCT Clinical AI Platform — owned-orchestration clinical AI',
    description: 'Case study of a clinician-facing AI chatbot and decision-support platform built under Sang Truong’s Head of AI role at EPIC TECHNOLOGY for Ho Chi Minh City Traditional Medicine Hospital, using a V4 owned-orchestration boundary, PostgreSQL Evidence Workspace, bounded local-corpus research, deterministic clinical authority, conditional claim/evidence verification, and protected-UAT acceptance.',
    dateModified: '2026-09-01T16:04:00+07:00',
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Sang Truong', url: new URL(withBase('/about'), Astro.site).href },
    mainEntityOfPage: canonical,
    about: ['Clinical AI', 'AI agents', 'RAG', 'FastAPI', 'Next.js', 'PostgreSQL', 'Qdrant', 'Protected UAT'],
  },
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL(withBase('/'), Astro.site).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'YHCT Clinical AI Platform', item: canonical },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="YHCT Clinical AI Platform — V4 Clinical AI Architecture | Sang Truong"
  description="Deep technical case study of the EPIC TECHNOLOGY project for Ho Chi Minh City Traditional Medicine Hospital: V4 owned orchestration, PostgreSQL Evidence Workspace, bounded local-corpus research, deterministic clinical authority, conditional verification, and protected-UAT acceptance."
  image="og-yhct.png"
  pageType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="case container section">
    <a class="back-link" href={withBase('#work')}>← Selected work</a>
    <header class="case-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case Study 01 · EPIC TECHNOLOGY · Clinical AI · 2026</p>
      <h1>YHCT Clinical AI Platform</h1>
      <p class="case-lede">Under my Head of Artificial Intelligence role at EPIC TECHNOLOGY, I architected and built the Ho Chi Minh City Traditional Medicine Hospital AI Chatbot & Clinical Decision-Support Platform: a clinician-facing system where the model owns semantic understanding and synthesis, while clinical facts, provenance, durable state, permissions, and publication safety remain explicit.</p>
      <div class="case-meta">
        <div><span>Role</span><strong>AI Architect / Lead Builder · EPIC TECHNOLOGY</strong></div>
        <div><span>Architecture</span><strong>V4 Clinical Notebook · owned orchestration</strong></div>
        <div><span>Stage</span><strong>Protected UAT accepted · clinician-feedback phase</strong></div>
      </div>
      <p class="case-verified">Architecture verified against the canonical V4 project state and architecture decision: <time datetime="2026-08-28">28 Aug 2026</time>.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="evidence-band" aria-label="Recorded validation evidence">
      <div><strong>338 passed</strong><span>focused backend validation on the owned-orchestration candidate</span></div>
      <div><strong>301 passed</strong><span>full V4 backend test set recorded by project state</span></div>
      <div><strong>Frontend green</strong><span>3 tests + lint + typecheck + production build</span></div>
      <div><strong>Protected UAT</strong><span>accepted on V4 owned orchestration; production/HIS not authorized</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section archify-section" aria-labelledby="architecture-map-title">
      <div class="archify-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Interactive architecture map</p>
          <h2 id="architecture-map-title">The current V4 runtime, not the earlier graph wrapper.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="archify-links">
          <a href={withBase('/yhct-v4-architecture.html')} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open fullscreen ↗</a>
          <a href={withBase('/yhct-v4.architecture.json')} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Archify JSON ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="archify-note">Built from the current YHCT V4 architecture using the Archify v2.13 typed architecture contract. The embedded map exposes focused views for the primary clinician turn, evidence research, and clinical-authority path.</p>
      <div class="archify-frame">
        <iframe
          src={withBase('/yhct-v4-architecture.html')}
          title="Interactive YHCT V4 Clinical Notebook architecture map"
          loading="lazy"
          sandbox="allow-scripts"
        ></iframe>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section case-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Problem</p><h2>Clinical AI cannot rely on fluent answers alone.</h2></div>
      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>A useful clinician assistant has to accept natural language, prescriptions, tables, and documents while keeping track of what it actually knows, which approved source or deterministic tool owns each fact, what state persists between turns, and what happens when evidence is incomplete or conflicting.</p>
        <p>The hard problem was not “add an LLM to a hospital UI.” It was designing useful semantic freedom without letting probabilistic prose silently become authoritative clinical logic.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule case-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">My ownership</p><h2>One explicit intelligence boundary on top of a proven hospital platform.</h2></div>
      <div class="ownership-list">
        <article><strong>V4 intelligence composition</strong><p>Consolidated model-visible wiring into <code>app.v4.composition</code>: Evidence Workspace context, research, observation recall, tool registry, model budget, and answer-publication policy. The shared platform chooses the V4 root but does not reassemble its internal intelligence pieces.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Clinical authority model</strong><p>Kept interaction findings, prescription findings, entity mappings, severity/rating fields, and approved release identity deterministic. The model can decide when to call tools and explain results, but cannot invert or override those facts.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Evidence and retrieval</strong><p>Made PostgreSQL canonical for conversation/evidence/audit state, with Qdrant treated as derived and rebuildable search state. Runtime research is bounded to the approved local corpus and selected evidence is rebound to canonical source/version metadata.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Publication and operational safety</strong><p>Moved answer breadth into the main FINAL decision, retained conditional claim/evidence verification where source-grounded prose requires it, and kept deterministic grounding guards, exact-SHA gates, explicit rollback, and protected-UAT boundaries.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule">
      <p class="eyebrow">Current runtime path</p>
      <div class="contract-grid">
        <div class="code-card"><span class="code-comment">// one model-visible composition root</span><strong>shared platform → app.v4.composition</strong><span class="code-comment">// mature bounded model → tool → observation → model kernel</span></div>
        <div class="principle-card"><span>MODEL</span><strong>language · reference resolution · research planning · answer scope</strong><span>APPLICATION / APPROVED DATA</span><strong>contracts · permissions · persistence · provenance · clinical facts</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule">
      <p class="eyebrow">Architecture decisions</p>
      <div class="decision-grid decision-grid-3">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Owned orchestration</h3><p><code>app.v4.composition</code> is the single V4 model-visible intelligence root. This removes overlapping control surfaces across Evidence Workspace, research, recall, publication, and verification.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>No ceremonial graph</h3><p>The former LangGraph runtime was only <code>START → execute_turn → END</code> and owned no meaningful branch, checkpoint, research, tool, or publication transition, so it was removed from the active protected-UAT path.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>PostgreSQL is canonical</h3><p>Conversations, durable turns, structured observations, Evidence Workspace state, claim/evidence references, publication metadata, audit, and ACL state remain canonical in PostgreSQL.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Qdrant is derived</h3><p>Vector/hybrid search state is rebuildable and cannot become a competing clinical memory truth. Evidence published to clinicians is rebound to authorized canonical source/version metadata.</p></article>
        <article><span>05</span><h3>Bounded local research</h3><p>Semantic planning can fan out across approved-corpus retrieval, dedupe and curate evidence, assess sufficiency, and perform at most one targeted refinement. Clinician runtime has no live-web fetch path.</p></article>
        <article><span>06</span><h3>Single-pass answer scope</h3><p>Answer breadth is part of the original FINAL instruction. The old post-hoc answer-contract model round and verifier scope-repair loop are removed; source-grounded prose gets conditional claim/evidence verification only when needed.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule case-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Evidence Workspace</p><h2>Conversation prose is context; persisted typed evidence is authority.</h2></div>
      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>V4 treats persisted structured observations and exact evidence handles as the authoritative memory available to semantic follow-up. Generic recall remains owner/conversation scoped; the system does not introduce one phrase-specific tool for each Vietnamese wording pattern.</p>
        <p>This is the key difference between “chat history as memory” and a clinical notebook: language remains flexible, while durable evidence and fact ownership stay inspectable.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule case-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Answer publication</p><h2>Extra model calls are conditional, not architectural ceremony.</h2></div>
      <div class="capability-grid">
        <article><h3>General / non-grounded</h3><p>The main-agent FINAL can go through deterministic application guards and publish without a second semantic classification round.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Deterministic clinical support</h3><p>Pure clinical-tool or compute-supported answers retain a verifier zero-extra-model-call fast path before deterministic grounding guards.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Corpus / document / mixed</h3><p>Source-grounded prose passes through the bounded claim/evidence verifier before publication when evidence semantics require it.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Persisted output</h3><p>Published answers keep citations, exact provenance and durable state rather than treating the model response as the system of record.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule case-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Current phase</p><h2>Protected UAT accepted; clinician feedback continues on the simpler boundary.</h2></div>
      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>The project state records the V4 owned-orchestration candidate as BigLinux validated and accepted in protected UAT, with semantic Vietnamese understanding, follow-up reference resolution, bounded agentic research, evidence sufficiency/refinement, narrow-answer behavior, multi-source synthesis, claim-to-evidence grounding, exact provenance, deterministic clinical authority, and durable evidence memory all recorded as implemented and correct for the protected-UAT path.</p>
        <p>Release-validation work such as a dedicated runtime cross-encoder reranker, full shadow-corpus reindex, broader benchmark campaigns, and post-stabilization optimization remains deliberately separate from the clinician runtime. Production and HIS remain out of scope.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule">
      <p class="eyebrow">Recorded validation state · 2026-08-28</p>
      <div class="status-table" role="table" aria-label="YHCT V4 validation status">
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Owned-orchestration protected UAT</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">Accepted</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Focused backend tests</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">338 passed</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Full V4 backend tests</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">301 passed</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Frontend validation</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">3 passed · lint · typecheck · production build</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Migration chain</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">0001 → 0025 · single head</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Semantic hardcode scan</span><strong role="cell" class="status-ok">Passed</strong></div>
        <div role="row"><span role="cell">Production / HIS authorization</span><strong role="cell">Not authorized · not claimed</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section demo-placeholder">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Public demo boundary</p>
        <h2>Sanitized proof, never hospital production.</h2>
        <p>A public demo should use synthetic prescriptions, sanitized knowledge, isolated credentials, no patient data, no production hospital integration, no private admin surface, and explicit rate limits. The protected hospital UAT environment itself is not the portfolio demo.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="status-pill">Demo not public yet</span>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .archify-section { padding-top: 22px; }
  .archify-heading { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:end; gap:28px; margin-bottom:12px; }
  .archify-heading h2 { margin:7px 0 0; max-width:780px; }
  .archify-links { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:9px; justify-content:flex-end; }
  .archify-links a { padding:9px 11px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:10px; color:var(--muted); font-size:.76rem; font-weight:700; text-decoration:none; }
  .archify-links a:hover { color:var(--text); border-color:rgba(32,184,255,.48); }
  .archify-note { max-width:880px; margin:0 0 18px; color:var(--muted); }
  .archify-frame { overflow:hidden; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:22px; background:#050913; box-shadow:0 28px 90px rgba(0,0,0,.24); }
  .archify-frame iframe { display:block; width:100%; height:820px; border:0; background:#050913; }
  code { font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,monospace; font-size:.92em; }
  @media (max-width:900px) {
    .archify-heading { align-items:flex-start; flex-direction:column; }
    .archify-links { justify-content:flex-start; }
    .archify-frame iframe { height:940px; }
  }
  @media (max-width:640px) {
    .archify-frame { margin-inline:-8px; border-radius:16px; }
    .archify-frame iframe { height:1120px; }
  }
</style>
